  DISCLOSURE — agency commit on minimal scenes
  123/132 belief solutions commit via a SCOPE complement (sync_except gv / sync_all) rather
  than sync_to_world(av).  On a scene whose only committed model-mover is the
  agent, 'move everything but the goal' == 'move the agent' — the two commits are
  extensionally identical (verified for every belief family).  It is the SAME
  fork-structured belief with the agency hole expressed on the goal rather than
  the actor, NOT a non-belief rival; counted as the agency commit above.
  For goal-displacement this is INTRINSIC, not sampled: on a two-value scene
  sync_except(gv) moves exactly {av}, so it IS sync_to_world(av) on every
  expressible scene.  Certified at construction (_goal_scope_certified): every
  OTHER scope complement fails per scene; the family whose scenes FORCE the
  literal spelling is false-obstacle, below.

  FORCED LITERAL COMMIT — false-obstacle family (degeneracy excluded by construction)
  9/24 false-obstacle tasks solved; commit forms: 9 literal, 0 degenerate, 0 multi-mover, 0 non-mental.
  Every solved one commits via the literal sync_to_world(av): no scope complement
  reproduces these scenes when paired with the derive this family certifies
  (real wall and goal stay put), so the agency commit is FORCED and found —
  not merely argued extensionally equal to a cheaper complement.

